adr: 0360
file: lib/dialect/pastoml.pas
kills: lib_toml_errors
why: Run goes back to being a function whose caller writes `ok := Run(false)`, so *did it read any digits* overwrites the refusal it had just recorded and `a = 1_` is accepted -- an underscore that is not between digits. It is the defect the module actually had for one draft, and it is the shape worth pinning: a routine that reports through a var parameter and also answers must not do both.
--- old
      else if Digit(Peek(b, i)) then
        Run(false)
--- new
      else if Digit(Peek(b, i)) then begin
        Run(false);
        ok := true
      end
